spec: specs/openapi.md stage 1, BACKLOG "openapi"

why: nothing in the tree declares what an operation ANSWERS — a
  handler builds `Response(200, …)` by hand — so every operation in
  the rendered document says "undeclared". It is the decider for
  whether a document is worth serving. TOUCHES okay-http (Route.scala),
  the optics-outside arc's file: that arc's eight stages are all
  landed, its spec plans no stage 9, the three `openapi-*` entries are
  unclaimed, I asked its owner twice in the room with no reply, and
  the operator said take it. Will say so in the room again on landing.

what: the declaration is the handler's TYPE, not an annotation beside
  it — `out`/`jsonOut` take a handler answering a VALUE, the router
  encodes it with the same `Schema` the document renders, so the two
  cannot drift. The router also declares the failures IT produces:
  `json[B]`'s own 400 for a body that does not parse. `Entry` gains
  the responses; okay-openapi renders them; "undeclared" stays for a
  handler that still builds its own `Response`.

next: Entry.responses, out/jsonOut, the 400 the router already emits,
  the renderer, tests both sides
